          "filename": "Gargoyle, castle buildings, Ludlow - geograph.org.uk - 1745726.jpg",
          "caption": "Gargoyle, castle buildings, Ludlow The word 'Gargoyle' derives from an old French word - gargouille- meaning 'throat'. A true gargoyle is a waterspout. An unusual carved creature that does not serve that purpose is called a \"Grotesque.\" The two are often confused. This one is located above the former prison on the edge of the outer bailey.",
